# Eliminating a `Remote`.
#
# `readyOr` legitimises discarding the loading state, which is the one
# thing §5.2's second invariant exists to prevent. It is a legal
# elimination of the variant, so the rule is satisfied to the letter, and
# forbidding it here would only make every program write it out by hand —
# which is §14F.2's own argument for having a library at all. It is
# included and flagged, not defended.

function readyOr with result, fallback
    when result
        Loading
            give fallback
        Failed with error
            give fallback
        Ready with value
            give value

function isReady of result
    when result
        Loading
            give no
        Failed with error
            give no
        Ready with value
            give yes
